From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: ROG5 train the lowest link rate that carries the mode (dp_link_policy)

msm (like stock msm-5.4, dp_ctrl_on) trains the maximum rate and lane count
the sink, the DT and the Type-C pin assignment allow, whatever the mode
needs: on the MSI MPG 491C (pin assignment C) 3840x1080@60 at 30 bpp
(266.5 MHz, 8.0 Gbit/s) runs on 4 lanes x HBR2 (17.28 Gbit/s payload).

What the link rate costs on SM8350: the DP controller votes its link clock
OPP (sm8350.dtsi dp_opp_table), MMCX SVS_L1 at 540 MHz (HBR2) but SVS at
270 MHz (HBR). With the DSI panel off, the DPU runs that mode at ~280 MHz
(0099 floor; 300 MHz OPP = SVS), so HBR2 alone lifts the MMCX rail to the
next corner. The link clock domain and the PHY serialisers also run at half
the rate at HBR. The lane count costs less: the PLL is shared, and in
2-lane mode qmp_v4_configure_dp_phy only lowers the bias of the unused TX
block. So 4 x HBR (8.64 Gbit/s, the mode at 92.5 %) is the cheapest link
for that mode; 2 x HBR2 has the same fill and carried it before 0136.

Pick the link like i915 (intel_dp_compute_link_config_wide: "max bpp, min
clock, min lanes") and amdgpu DC (decide_dp_link_settings): the lowest
standard rate that carries the mode, then the fewest lanes at that rate,
never fewer than 2 unless the link has only 1. The bpp stays what mode
validation chose for the maximum link. A reduced link must leave margin:
msm.dp_link_fill_pct (default 95 %: SSC downspread and reference clock
0.6 %, DP 2.1 2.6.4.1, plus transfer unit rounding). Nouveau and msm train
the maximum instead; i915 does so only for MST and for eDP before 1.4.

msm.dp_link_policy: 0 = maximum (old behaviour), 1 = lowest rate then fewest
lanes (default), 2 = fewest lanes then lowest rate (for A/B measurements:
2 x HBR2 for the mode above without a replug). Read at every link enable,
i.e. the next modeset; every mode change retrains, so a new mode gets its
own link. If the reduced link fails training (including running out of
retries, which msm's loop otherwise reports as success), or msm's downshifts
end on a link without the margin, it retrains at the maximum exactly as
before (inherited: those downshifts, and CTS link-training requests, which
change link_params without retraining the PHY). External DP with
standard rates only (no eDP, no eDP 1.4 rate table); a PHY compliance test
keeps its link. Mode validation and bpp selection still use the maximum
link (0110 converter cap, 0137 pin assignment lanes, 0138 HBR3/lane caps,
msm.dp_max_rate).

Expected: MMCX SVS instead of SVS_L1 and half the link clock for that mode,
tens of mW (measurement: scripts/device/rog5-dp-power-measure). 4 x HBR is
new on this port and monitor: check the picture and the policy line in the
kernel log after the first enable; msm.dp_link_policy=0 plus a modeset puts
the old link back.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -2389,56 +2389,121 @@
 	return drm_dp_channel_eq_ok(link_status, num_lanes);
 }
 
-int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl)
+/*
+ * ROG5: link configuration policy. Mainline msm, like stock msm-5.4, trains
+ * the most the sink and the Type-C pin assignment allow: 4 lanes x HBR2
+ * (17.28 Gbit/s payload) for 3840x1080@60 at 30 bpp (8.0 Gbit/s) on the MSI
+ * MPG 491C. The DP controller's link clock OPP (sm8350.dtsi dp_opp_table)
+ * needs MMCX SVS_L1 at HBR2 (540 MHz) but SVS at HBR (270 MHz), the corner
+ * the DPU holds anyway for such a mode (core clock ~280 MHz, 300 MHz OPP),
+ * and the link clock domain and the PHY serialisers run at half the rate.
+ * So, in the order of i915 (intel_dp_compute_link_config_wide: "max bpp,
+ * min clock, min lanes") and amdgpu DC (decide_dp_link_settings), train the
+ * lowest rate that carries the mode and, at that rate, the fewest lanes
+ * (not below 2: a single lane is untested here and saves nothing
+ * measurable). The bpp stays what mode validation chose for the maximum
+ * link (msm_dp_panel_get_mode_bpp), as i915 keeps the maximum bpp.
+ *
+ *   dp_link_policy=0  maximum rate and lanes (mainline and stock behaviour)
+ *   dp_link_policy=1  lowest rate, then fewest lanes (default)
+ *   dp_link_policy=2  fewest lanes, then lowest rate (A/B tests: 2 x HBR2
+ *                     for the mode above without a replug)
+ *   dp_link_fill_pct  a reduced link carries the mode only if the mode needs
+ *                     at most this share of its payload bandwidth (50-100,
+ *                     default 95: 0.6 % SSC downspread and reference clock
+ *                     margin, DP 2.1 2.6.4.1, plus transfer unit rounding;
+ *                     2 x HBR2 has carried 3840x1080@60 30 bpp at 92.5 %)
+ *
+ * Both are read at every link enable, i.e. at the next modeset (every mode
+ * change retrains). A reduced link that fails training, or that trains only
+ * after msm's own downshifts to a link that no longer carries the mode, is
+ * retrained at the maximum. External DP with standard rates only (no eDP,
+ * no eDP 1.4 rate tables); PHY compliance test requests keep their link.
+ */
+static uint msm_dp_link_policy = 1;
+module_param_named(dp_link_policy, msm_dp_link_policy, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_link_policy, "ROG5: DP link config at the next modeset: 0 = max rate and lanes, 1 = lowest rate then fewest lanes (default), 2 = fewest lanes then lowest rate");
+static uint msm_dp_link_fill_pct = 95;
+module_param_named(dp_link_fill_pct, msm_dp_link_fill_pct, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_link_fill_pct, "ROG5: largest share (%) of a reduced DP link's payload bandwidth a mode may use (50-100, default 95)");
+
+/* 8b/10b: rate is the symbol rate in kHz, 8 payload bits per symbol and lane */
+static bool msm_dp_ctrl_link_carries(u32 lanes, u32 rate, u64 need_kbps,
+				     u32 fill_pct)
 {
-	int rc = 0;
-	struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl;
-	u32 rate;
-	int link_train_max_retries = 5;
-	u32 const phy_cts_pixel_clk_khz = 148500;
-	u8 link_status[DP_LINK_STATUS_SIZE];
-	unsigned int training_step;
-	unsigned long pixel_rate;
+	return need_kbps * 100 <= (u64)lanes * rate * 8 * fill_pct;
+}
 
-	if (!msm_dp_ctrl)
-		return -EINVAL;
+/*
+ * link_params holds the maximum link (rate, lanes). Replace it with the one
+ * dp_link_policy picks for need_kbps; true when that is below the maximum.
+ */
+static bool msm_dp_ctrl_pick_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl,
+				  u64 need_kbps)
+{
+	static const u32 rates[] = { 162000, 270000, 540000, 810000 };
+	struct msm_dp_link_info *params = &ctrl->link->link_params;
+	u32 max_rate = params->rate, max_lanes = params->num_lanes;
+	u32 min_lanes = min_t(u32, 2, max_lanes);
+	u32 policy = READ_ONCE(msm_dp_link_policy);
+	u32 fill = clamp_t(u32, READ_ONCE(msm_dp_link_fill_pct), 50, 100);
+	u32 lanes;
+	int i;
+
+	if (policy != 1 && policy != 2)
+		return false;
+	if (!need_kbps || !min_lanes ||
+	    ctrl->panel->dpcd[DP_EDP_CONFIGURATION_CAP] ||
+	    ctrl->panel->link_info.use_rate_set)
+		return false;
+
+	if (policy == 1) {
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rates) && rates[i] <= max_rate; i++)
+			for (lanes = min_lanes; lanes <= max_lanes; lanes <<= 1)
+				if (msm_dp_ctrl_link_carries(lanes, rates[i],
+							     need_kbps, fill))
+					goto found;
+	} else {
+		for (lanes = min_lanes; lanes <= max_lanes; lanes <<= 1)
+			for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rates) && rates[i] <= max_rate; i++)
+				if (msm_dp_ctrl_link_carries(lanes, rates[i],
+							     need_kbps, fill))
+					goto found;
+	}
 
-	ctrl = container_of(msm_dp_ctrl, struct msm_dp_ctrl_private, msm_dp_ctrl);
+	return false;
 
-	rate = ctrl->panel->link_info.rate;
-	if (msm_dp_max_rate && rate > msm_dp_max_rate)
-		rate = msm_dp_max_rate;
-	pixel_rate = ctrl->panel->msm_dp_mode.drm_mode.clock;
+found:
+	if (rates[i] == max_rate && lanes == max_lanes)
+		return false;
 
-	msm_dp_ctrl_core_clk_enable(&ctrl->msm_dp_ctrl);
+	params->rate = rates[i];
+	params->num_lanes = lanes;
 
-	if (ctrl->link->sink_request & DP_TEST_LINK_PHY_TEST_PATTERN) {
-		drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev,
-				"using phy test link parameters\n");
-		if (!pixel_rate)
-			pixel_rate = phy_cts_pixel_clk_khz;
-	} else {
-		ctrl->link->link_params.rate = rate;
-		ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes =
-			ctrl->panel->link_info.num_lanes;
-		if (ctrl->panel->msm_dp_mode.out_fmt_is_yuv_420)
-			pixel_rate >>= 1;
-	}
-
-	drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev, "rate=%d, num_lanes=%d, pixel_rate=%lu\n",
-		ctrl->link->link_params.rate, ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes,
-		pixel_rate);
+	return true;
+}
 
-	rc = msm_dp_ctrl_enable_mainlink_clocks(ctrl);
-	if (rc)
-		return rc;
+/*
+ * Link training with msm's rate and lane downshifts on failure. Inherited:
+ * when the retries run out, rc is the last (successful) reinitialisation,
+ * i.e. 0 for a link that never trained; on_stream() retrains it once more.
+ * ROG5: strict (a reduced link, 0145) reports that as -ETIMEDOUT so the
+ * caller falls back to the maximum link; the maximum link keeps the old flow.
+ */
+static int msm_dp_ctrl_train_link_downshift(struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl,
+					    bool strict)
+{
+	int rc = 0;
+	int link_train_max_retries = 5;
+	u8 link_status[DP_LINK_STATUS_SIZE];
+	unsigned int training_step;
 
 	while (--link_train_max_retries) {
 		training_step = DP_TRAINING_NONE;
 		rc = msm_dp_ctrl_setup_main_link(ctrl, &training_step);
 		if (rc == 0) {
 			/* training completed successfully */
-			break;
+			return 0;
 		} else if (training_step == DP_TRAINING_1) {
 			/* link train_1 failed */
 			if (!msm_dp_aux_is_link_connected(ctrl->aux))
@@ -2493,6 +2558,96 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (strict && !rc)
+		rc = -ETIMEDOUT;
+
+	return rc;
+}
+
+int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl)
+{
+	int rc = 0;
+	struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl;
+	u32 rate, max_lanes = 0;
+	u32 const phy_cts_pixel_clk_khz = 148500;
+	unsigned long pixel_rate;
+	u64 need_kbps = 0;
+	bool reduced = false;
+
+	if (!msm_dp_ctrl)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	ctrl = container_of(msm_dp_ctrl, struct msm_dp_ctrl_private, msm_dp_ctrl);
+
+	rate = ctrl->panel->link_info.rate;
+	if (msm_dp_max_rate && rate > msm_dp_max_rate)
+		rate = msm_dp_max_rate;
+	pixel_rate = ctrl->panel->msm_dp_mode.drm_mode.clock;
+
+	msm_dp_ctrl_core_clk_enable(&ctrl->msm_dp_ctrl);
+
+	if (ctrl->link->sink_request & DP_TEST_LINK_PHY_TEST_PATTERN) {
+		drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev,
+				"using phy test link parameters\n");
+		if (!pixel_rate)
+			pixel_rate = phy_cts_pixel_clk_khz;
+	} else {
+		max_lanes = ctrl->panel->link_info.num_lanes;
+		ctrl->link->link_params.rate = rate;
+		ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes = max_lanes;
+		if (ctrl->panel->msm_dp_mode.out_fmt_is_yuv_420)
+			pixel_rate >>= 1;
+
+		/* ROG5: dp_link_policy (see msm_dp_ctrl_pick_link) */
+		need_kbps = (u64)pixel_rate * ctrl->panel->msm_dp_mode.bpp;
+		reduced = msm_dp_ctrl_pick_link(ctrl, need_kbps);
+		if (reduced)
+			drm_info(ctrl->drm_dev,
+				 "DP: link policy %u: %u lanes x %u kHz for %llu kbit/s (max %u x %u)\n",
+				 READ_ONCE(msm_dp_link_policy),
+				 ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes,
+				 ctrl->link->link_params.rate, need_kbps,
+				 max_lanes, rate);
+	}
+
+	drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev, "rate=%d, num_lanes=%d, pixel_rate=%lu\n",
+		ctrl->link->link_params.rate, ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes,
+		pixel_rate);
+
+	rc = msm_dp_ctrl_enable_mainlink_clocks(ctrl);
+	if (rc && !reduced)
+		return rc;
+
+	if (!rc)
+		rc = msm_dp_ctrl_train_link_downshift(ctrl, reduced);
+
+	/*
+	 * ROG5: a reduced link that failed, or that msm's downshifts left
+	 * without the policy's margin: retrain at the maximum, exactly as
+	 * before the policy (including its inherited downshifts, which can end
+	 * below the mode's bandwidth).
+	 */
+	if (reduced &&
+	    (rc || !msm_dp_ctrl_link_carries(ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes,
+					     ctrl->link->link_params.rate, need_kbps,
+					     clamp_t(u32, READ_ONCE(msm_dp_link_fill_pct),
+						     50, 100))) &&
+	    msm_dp_aux_is_link_connected(ctrl->aux)) {
+		drm_info(ctrl->drm_dev,
+			 "DP: link policy: %u lanes x %u kHz %s (rc=%d), training %u lanes x %u kHz\n",
+			 ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes,
+			 ctrl->link->link_params.rate,
+			 rc ? "failed" : "too small for the mode", rc,
+			 max_lanes, rate);
+		ctrl->link->link_params.rate = rate;
+		ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes = max_lanes;
+		rc = msm_dp_ctrl_reinitialize_mainlink(ctrl);
+		if (rc)
+			DRM_ERROR("Failed to reinitialize mainlink. rc=%d\n", rc);
+		else
+			rc = msm_dp_ctrl_train_link_downshift(ctrl, false);
+	}
+
 	if (ctrl->link->sink_request & DP_TEST_LINK_PHY_TEST_PATTERN)
 		return rc;
 
